<title>HUNGARY: Hungary details May CPI figures.</title>
<headline>Hungary details May CPI figures.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Central Statistical Office (KSH) released detailed May consumer price index (CPI) figures on Wednesday.</p>
<p>CPI PCT CHANGE IN MAIN PRODUCT GROUPS</p>
<p>				   May 1997		Weight in</p>
<p>				mth/mth   yr/yr	   index (pct)</p>
<p> Food products		2.6     16.9	     28.6</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages and</p>
<p> tobacco products	   1.3     20.0		9.0</p>
<p> Clothing		     1.3     18.9		6.3</p>
<p> Durable consumer goods   0.5	7.8		6.2</p>
<p> Household energy	   0.4     24.9		8.0</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels	 0.2     15.2	     17.0</p>
<p> Services		     1.0     18.7	     24.9</p>
<p> Total			  1.3     17.7	    100.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The CPI was boosted by government measures by 0.1 percent within the total 1.3 percent month-on-month rise in April, the KSH said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
